   "source": [
    "# Effective Python Patterns for ML Engineers\n",
    "## 25 Core Patterns You'll Actually Use\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook covers **patterns you'll hit constantly** in neural networks and ML projects. Each section:\n",
    "1. **Why You Care** — where this matters in ML\n",
    "2. **The Problem** — concrete scenario\n",
    "3. **Bad Code** — what happens without the pattern\n",
    "4. **Good Code** — the pattern applied\n",
    "5. **Your Turn** — practice exercise\n",
    "6. **Reflection** — when you'd use this in your neural net\n",
    "\n",
    "**Time per section:** 10-15 minutes. Work through 1-2 per session.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# PART 1: PYTHONIC ITERATION\n",
    "## These are your bread and butter for loops."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pattern 1: Enumerate Over Range (Don't Use Range)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "You're iterating through training data, epochs, layers. You need **both the index and the value**. Most people reach for `range(len(...))` and it's ugly.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You have a list of loss values per epoch. You want to print each loss with its epoch number."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bad Code: Using range(len(...))\n",
    "losses = [0.5, 0.45, 0.42, 0.41]\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(len(losses)):\n",
    "    epoch = i + 1\n",
    "    loss = losses[i]\n",
    "    print(f\"Epoch {epoch}: Loss = {loss}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Problems with that code:**\n",
    "- Verbose and hard to read\n",
    "- Off-by-one errors (why `i + 1`?)\n",
    "- Slower (length lookup, index lookup)\n",
    "- Doesn't work with iterators (generators)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Good Code: Using enumerate()\n",
    "losses = [0.5, 0.45, 0.42, 0.41]\n",
    "\n",
    "for epoch, loss in enumerate(losses, start=1):  # start=1 makes epochs 1-indexed\n",
    "    print(f\"Epoch {epoch}: Loss = {loss}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Why this is better:**\n",
    "- Crystal clear intent\n",
    "- Works with any iterable (lists, generators, file handles)\n",
    "- `start=` parameter handles the offset cleanly\n",
    "- Faster (no index lookup)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your Turn: Practice\n",
    "\n",
    "You have a batch of data samples and their labels. Print each one with its position in the batch (1-indexed).\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "batch_data = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]\n",
    "labels = ['cat', 'dog', 'cat']\n",
    "\n",
    "# TODO: Use enumerate to print:\n",
    "# Sample 1: [1, 2, 3] -> cat\n",
    "# Sample 2: [4, 5, 6] -> dog\n",
    "# Sample 3: [7, 8, 9] -> cat\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hint:** You can enumerate over two iterables at once by zipping them first."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Your code here\n",
    "batch_data = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]\n",
    "labels = ['cat', 'dog', 'cat']\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Reflection: In Your Neural Network\n",
    "\n",
    "You'll use this constantly:\n",
    "- Iterating through training data: `for batch_idx, (X, y) in enumerate(data_loader):`\n",
    "- Printing progress: `for layer_idx, layer in enumerate(self.layers):`\n",
    "- Debugging: `for step, loss in enumerate(training_losses):`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Pattern 2: Zip for Parallel Iteration\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "You often have multiple related sequences: features and labels, weights and biases, layer sizes and activation functions. You want to iterate through them **in parallel**, not separately.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You have features and labels (from a training batch). You want to process each sample-label pair together."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bad Code: Manual indexing\n",
    "features = [[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]]\n",
    "labels = [0, 1, 0]\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(len(features)):\n",
    "    feature = features[i]\n",
    "    label = labels[i]\n",
    "    print(f\"Feature: {feature}, Label: {label}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Good Code: Using zip()\n",
    "features = [[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]]\n",
    "labels = [0, 1, 0]\n",
    "\n",
    "for feature, label in zip(features, labels):\n",
    "    print(f\"Feature: {feature}, Label: {label}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Why this is better:**\n",
    "- No manual indexing, no off-by-one errors\n",
    "- Works with iterables of different types (lists, generators, numpy arrays)\n",
    "- Stops at the shortest iterable automatically (safe)\n",
    "- Can zip 2, 3, or more things: `zip(a, b, c, d)`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your Turn: Practice\n",
    "\n",
    "You have layer sizes and activation functions. Print them together.\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "layer_sizes = [784, 128, 64, 10]\n",
    "activations = ['input', 'relu', 'relu', 'softmax']\n",
    "\n",
    "# TODO: Use zip to print:\n",
    "# Layer 1: 784 neurons, activation=input\n",
    "# Layer 2: 128 neurons, activation=relu\n",
    "# ...\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Your code here\n",
    "layer_sizes = [784, 128, 64, 10]\n",
    "activations = ['input', 'relu', 'relu', 'softmax']\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Reflection: In Your Neural Network\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# Forward pass through layers\n",
    "x = input_data\n",
    "for layer, activation in zip(self.layers, self.activations):\n",
    "    x = layer(x)\n",
    "    x = activation(x)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Matching weights and biases\n",
    "for weight, bias in zip(self.weights, self.biases):\n",
    "    # update them together\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Pattern 3: List/Dict/Set Comprehensions\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "You're constantly transforming data: normalizing features, extracting columns, filtering samples. Comprehensions are **faster, clearer, and more Pythonic** than loops.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You have raw feature values. You want to normalize them (divide by max)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bad Code: Manual loop and append\n",
    "features = [10, 20, 15, 25, 30]\n",
    "max_feature = max(features)\n",
    "\n",
    "normalized = []\n",
    "for f in features:\n",
    "    normalized.append(f / max_feature)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(normalized)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Good Code: List comprehension\n",
    "features = [10, 20, 15, 25, 30]\n",
    "max_feature = max(features)\n",
    "\n",
    "normalized = [f / max_feature for f in features]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(normalized)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Why this is better:**\n",
    "- One line instead of three\n",
    "- Faster (single statement, no repeated `append` calls)\n",
    "- Clearer intent (transform this into that)\n",
    "- Can add conditions: `[f / max_feature for f in features if f > 10]`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Filtering with Comprehensions\n",
    "\n",
    "You often need to filter too:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Get only positive values\n",
    "values = [1, -2, 3, -4, 5]\n",
    "positive = [v for v in values if v > 0]\n",
    "print(positive)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Dict Comprehensions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bad Code: Manual dict building\n",
    "layer_names = ['input', 'hidden', 'output']\n",
    "layer_sizes = [784, 128, 10]\n",
    "\n",
    "config = {}\n",
    "for name, size in zip(layer_names, layer_sizes):\n",
    "    config[name] = size\n",
    "\n",
    "print(config)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Good Code: Dict comprehension\n",
    "layer_names = ['input', 'hidden', 'output']\n",
    "layer_sizes = [784, 128, 10]\n",
    "\n",
    "config = {name: size for name, size in zip(layer_names, layer_sizes)}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(config)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your Turn: Practice\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **List comprehension:** You have raw image pixel values (0-255). Normalize them to 0-1.\n",
    "   ```python\n",
    "   pixels = [0, 128, 255, 64]\n",
    "   # TODO: normalized = ...\n",
    "   ```\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Filtering:** Keep only pixels above 100.\n",
    "   ```python\n",
    "   pixels = [0, 128, 255, 64]\n",
    "   # TODO: bright_pixels = ...\n",
    "   ```\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Dict comprehension:** Create a dict mapping parameter names to their initial values.\n",
    "   ```python\n",
    "   param_names = ['weight_1', 'bias_1', 'weight_2']\n",
    "   initial_values = [0.01, 0.0, 0.01]\n",
    "   # TODO: params = ...\n",
    "   ```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Your code here\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Normalize pixels\n",
    "pixels = [0, 128, 255, 64]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Filter bright pixels\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Dict comprehension\n",
    "param_names = ['weight_1', 'bias_1', 'weight_2']\n",
    "initial_values = [0.01, 0.0, 0.01]\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Reflection: In Your Neural Network\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# Normalize training data\n",
    "X_normalized = [(x - mean) / std for x in X_train]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter outliers\n",
