    "layer_config = {f\"layer_{i}\": size for i, size in enumerate(layer_sizes)}\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# PART 2: FUNCTION ARGUMENTS & UNPACKING\n",
    "## Making functions flexible and readable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pattern 4: Default Arguments (But Watch Out)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "Most function calls use the same arguments. Default arguments make code cleaner. **But there's a trap with mutable defaults.**\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You're creating a neural network layer. Most calls use the same activation. You want a default."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Good Code: Default arguments\n",
    "def create_layer(input_size, output_size, activation='relu'):\n",
    "    return {\"input_size\": input_size, \"output_size\": output_size, \"activation\": activation}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Call with defaults\n",
    "layer1 = create_layer(784, 128)\n",
    "print(layer1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Override when needed\n",
    "layer2 = create_layer(128, 10, activation='softmax')\n",
    "print(layer2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### ⚠️ THE TRAP: Mutable Default Arguments\n",
    "\n",
    "**Never use mutable objects as defaults** (lists, dicts, sets). They're shared across all calls!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# DANGEROUS CODE: Mutable default\n",
    "def add_to_list(item, my_list=[]):\n",
    "    my_list.append(item)\n",
    "    return my_list\n",
    "\n",
    "result1 = add_to_list(1)\n",
    "print(f\"Call 1: {result1}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "result2 = add_to_list(2)\n",
    "print(f\"Call 2: {result2}\")  # SURPRISE: Contains 1 AND 2!\n",
    "\n",
    "result3 = add_to_list(3)\n",
    "print(f\"Call 3: {result3}\")  # Now has 1, 2, AND 3!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The default list is created **once** when the function is defined, not each time it's called. All calls share the same list.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Fix: Use `None` as the default, then create a new object inside the function.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# GOOD CODE: None as default, then initialize\n",
    "def add_to_list(item, my_list=None):\n",
    "    if my_list is None:\n",
    "        my_list = []\n",
    "    my_list.append(item)\n",
    "    return my_list\n",
    "\n",
    "result1 = add_to_list(1)\n",
    "print(f\"Call 1: {result1}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "result2 = add_to_list(2)\n",
    "print(f\"Call 2: {result2}\")  # Now correct: only [2]\n",
    "\n",
    "result3 = add_to_list(3)\n",
    "print(f\"Call 3: {result3}\")  # Only [3]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your Turn: Practice\n",
    "\n",
    "What's wrong with this neural net initialization code? Fix it.\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "def create_network(layer_sizes, activation_functions=[]):\n",
    "    # Build network with these layer sizes and activations\n",
    "    if not activation_functions:\n",
    "        activation_functions.append('relu')\n",
    "    # ...\n",
    "    return activation_functions\n",
    "\n",
    "net1 = create_network([784, 128, 10])\n",
    "net2 = create_network([50, 25, 5])\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "What happens when you call `net1` and then `net2`? Why?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# First, show the bug:\n",
    "def create_network_BUGGY(layer_sizes, activation_functions=[]):\n",
    "    if not activation_functions:\n",
    "        activation_functions.append('relu')\n",
    "    return activation_functions\n",
    "\n",
    "net1 = create_network_BUGGY([784, 128, 10])\n",
    "print(f\"net1: {net1}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "net2 = create_network_BUGGY([50, 25, 5])\n",
    "print(f\"net2: {net2}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Now fix it:\n",
    "def create_network_FIXED(layer_sizes, activation_functions=None):\n",
    "    if activation_functions is None:\n",
    "        activation_functions = []\n",
    "    if not activation_functions:\n",
    "        activation_functions.append('relu')\n",
    "    return activation_functions\n",
    "\n",
    "net1 = create_network_FIXED([784, 128, 10])\n",
    "print(f\"net1 (fixed): {net1}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "net2 = create_network_FIXED([50, 25, 5])\n",
    "print(f\"net2 (fixed): {net2}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Reflection: In Your Neural Network\n",
    "\n",
    "This bug will **definitely** bite you if you're not careful:\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# BAD: Shared layer list across all networks\n",
    "def __init__(self, layer_sizes, layers=[]):\n",
    "    self.layers = layers  # DANGER!\n",
    "\n",
    "# GOOD: Create fresh list each time\n",
    "def __init__(self, layer_sizes, layers=None):\n",
    "    self.layers = layers if layers is not None else []\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Pattern 5: Keyword-Only Arguments\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "Some arguments are so important that you want to force the caller to be explicit. Keyword-only arguments make code **self-documenting**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You have a training function with lots of hyperparameters. You want to prevent accidental ordering mistakes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bad Code: Positional arguments (confusing which is which)\n",
    "def train(model, data, 0.001, 32, 100, True):\n",
    "    # What does each argument mean?\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "# Easy to mess up:\n",
    "# train(model, data, 0.001, 32, 100, True)  # Correct?\n",
    "# train(model, data, 32, 0.001, 100, True)  # Wrong but hard to spot!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Good Code: Keyword-only arguments (after *)\n",
    "def train(model, data, *, learning_rate=0.001, batch_size=32, epochs=100, verbose=True):\n",
    "    print(f\"Training with lr={learning_rate}, batch={batch_size}, epochs={epochs}\")\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "# Now you must be explicit:\n",
    "train(model, data)  # Uses all defaults\n",
    "train(model, data, learning_rate=0.01, epochs=50)  # Crystal clear\n",
    "train(model, data, batch_size=64)  # Changes only batch size"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Why this is better:**\n",
    "- Self-documenting (you see the parameter name at the call site)\n",
    "- Can't mix up argument order\n",
    "- Obvious what's being overridden"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your Turn: Practice\n",
    "\n",
    "Rewrite this function to use keyword-only arguments:\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "def initialize_layer(input_size, output_size, 0.01, 'normal'):\n",
    "    # Builds a layer with:\n",
    "    # - input_size: number of inputs\n",
    "    # - output_size: number of neurons\n",
    "    # - 0.01: weight scale (std dev for initialization)\n",
    "    # - 'normal': initialization method ('normal' or 'uniform')\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "What should the fixed version look like?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Your code here\n",
    "def initialize_layer(input_size, output_size, *, weight_scale=0.01, init_method='normal'):\n",
    "    print(f\"Layer: {input_size} -> {output_size}, scale={weight_scale}, method={init_method}\")\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test it\n",
    "initialize_layer(784, 128)  # Defaults\n",
    "initialize_layer(784, 128, weight_scale=0.001)  # Override one\n",
    "initialize_layer(784, 128, init_method='uniform', weight_scale=0.01)  # Override in any order"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Pattern 6: *args and **kwargs\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "Sometimes you need to pass a variable number of arguments, or forward arguments to another function. `*args` and `**kwargs` let you do that.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You're building a neural network. Layers take different arguments. You want a flexible function that can pass arguments to the layer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# *args: Variable positional arguments\n",
    "def print_losses(*losses):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Print any number of losses.\"\"\"\n",
    "    for i, loss in enumerate(losses, start=1):\n",
    "        print(f\"Loss {i}: {loss}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print_losses(0.5)  # One loss\n",
    "print_losses(0.5, 0.4, 0.3)  # Three losses\n",
    "print_losses(0.5, 0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1)  # Five losses"
   ]
