    "---\n",
    "## Pattern 7: Unpacking (Assignment Expressions)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "You often need to extract elements from tuples or lists. Unpacking makes it clean.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You're loading a batch: `batch = (features, labels, metadata)`. You want to extract each."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bad Code: Manual indexing\n",
    "batch = ([1, 2, 3], [0, 1, 0], {'size': 3})\n",
    "\n",
    "features = batch[0]\n",
    "labels = batch[1]\n",
    "metadata = batch[2]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Features: {features}, Labels: {labels}\")"
   ]
  },
