    "---\n",
    "# PART 3: CLASSES & OBJECT-ORIENTED DESIGN\n",
    "## Building clean, maintainable code."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pattern 8: Proper Class Initialization (`__init__`)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "Your neural network **is** a class. Getting `__init__` right sets the foundation for everything.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You have a neural network with weights, biases, activation functions. How do you initialize all of that?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Good Code: Proper __init__\n",
    "class SimpleNeuralNet:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, layer_sizes, learning_rate=0.01):\n",
    "        \"\"\"Initialize network with given layer sizes.\n",
    "        \n",
    "        Args:\n",
    "            layer_sizes: List like [784, 128, 64, 10] (input -> hidden -> output)\n",
    "            learning_rate: Learning rate for gradient descent\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        self.layer_sizes = layer_sizes\n",
    "        self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n",
    "        self.weights = []\n",
    "        self.biases = []\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Initialize weights and biases\n",
    "        for i in range(len(layer_sizes) - 1):\n",
    "            w = np.random.randn(layer_sizes[i], layer_sizes[i + 1]) * 0.01\n",
    "            b = np.zeros((1, layer_sizes[i + 1]))\n",
    "            self.weights.append(w)\n",
    "            self.biases.append(b)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def __repr__(self):\n",
    "        return f\"SimpleNeuralNet(layers={self.layer_sizes}, lr={self.learning_rate})\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Now you can create networks easily\n",
    "net = SimpleNeuralNet([784, 128, 64, 10], learning_rate=0.01)\n",
    "print(net)\n",
    "print(f\"Weights shape: {[w.shape for w in net.weights]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Why This Matters\n",
    "- **`__init__` stores configuration** so you can reference it later\n",
    "- **Docstrings** explain what the arguments do\n",
    "- **`__repr__`** makes debugging easier (you see the object's state when you print it)\n",
    "- **Avoids mutable defaults** (we're careful about that)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
