   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Pattern 9: @property Decorators\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "Sometimes you want to compute a value on-the-fly (like network accuracy), but access it like an attribute (not a method). `@property` lets you do that.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "Your network has weights and biases. You want to compute the total number of parameters. Should it be a method or an attribute?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bad Code: Confusing API\n",
    "class NeuralNet:\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        self.weights = [np.ones((10, 20)), np.ones((20, 5))]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def get_param_count(self):  # Is this an attribute or a method?\n",
    "        return sum(w.size for w in self.weights)\n",
    "\n",
    "net = NeuralNet()\n",
    "count = net.get_param_count()  # Must remember to call it as a method\n",
    "print(count)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Good Code: Using @property\n",
    "class NeuralNet:\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        self.weights = [np.ones((10, 20)), np.ones((20, 5))]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @property\n",
    "    def param_count(self):  # Computed on access, no parentheses needed\n",
    "        return sum(w.size for w in self.weights)\n",
    "\n",
    "net = NeuralNet()\n",
    "count = net.param_count  # Access like an attribute\n",
    "print(count)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Why this is better:**\n",
    "- Cleaner API: `net.param_count` vs `net.get_param_count()`\n",
    "- Computed on access (lazy evaluation)\n",
    "- Can add validation/logic without changing the call site"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": {"\"type\": \"code\", \"source\": []}, "metadata": {}
   },
   "source": [
    "# More examples\n",
    "class Layer:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, input_size, output_size):\n",
    "        self.weights = np.random.randn(input_size, output_size)\n",
    "        self.biases = np.zeros((1, output_size))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @property\n",
    "    def weight_shape(self):\n",
    "        return self.weights.shape\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @property\n",
    "    def total_parameters(self):\n",
    "        return self.weights.size + self.biases.size\n",
    "\n",
    "layer = Layer(10, 5)\n",
    "print(f\"Shape: {layer.weight_shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Parameters: {layer.total_parameters}\")"
   ]
