   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# PART 4: GENERATORS & ITERATION\n",
    "## Memory-efficient data processing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pattern 10: Generators (yield)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "With big datasets, you can't load everything into memory. Generators produce values **one at a time**, keeping memory usage low.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You have a large dataset. You want to iterate through batches without loading the entire dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bad Code: Load everything into a list (memory hog)\n",
    "def load_batches_BAD(data, batch_size):\n",
    "    batches = []\n",
    "    for i in range(0, len(data), batch_size):\n",
    "        batch = data[i:i+batch_size]\n",
    "        batches.append(batch)  # Store everything in memory\n",
    "    return batches\n",
    "\n",
    "data = list(range(1000))\n",
    "batches = load_batches_BAD(data, 32)  # All 1000 elements + all batches in memory\n",
    "print(f\"Number of batches: {len(batches)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Good Code: Generator (memory efficient)\n",
    "def load_batches_GOOD(data, batch_size):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Yield batches one at a time.\"\"\"\n",
    "    for i in range(0, len(data), batch_size):\n",
    "        batch = data[i:i+batch_size]\n",
    "        yield batch  # Produce one batch, pause execution\n",
    "\n",
    "data = list(range(1000))\n",
    "batch_gen = load_batches_GOOD(data, 32)  # Nothing computed yet\n",
    "\n",
    "# Iterate through batches as needed\n",
    "for batch in batch_gen:\n",
    "    print(f\"Batch: {batch[:5]}...\")  # Only one batch in memory at a time\n",
    "    if batch == [96, 97, 98]:  # Stop early if you want\n",
    "        break"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### How Generators Work\n",
    "\n",
    "- **`yield`** pauses the function and returns a value\n",
    "- The next time you call `next()` (or iterate), execution **resumes** right after the yield\n",
    "- Perfect for lazy evaluation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Simple generator example\n",
    "def count_to_three():\n",
    "    print(\"Starting\")\n",
    "    yield 1\n",
    "    print(\"Between 1 and 2\")\n",
    "    yield 2\n",
    "    print(\"Between 2 and 3\")\n",
    "    yield 3\n",
    "    print(\"Done\")\n",
    "\n",
    "gen = count_to_three()\n",
    "print(next(gen))  # Prints \"Starting\", then 1\n",
    "print(next(gen))  # Prints \"Between 1 and 2\", then 2\n",
    "print(next(gen))  # Prints \"Between 2 and 3\", then 3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
