    "#     break"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Pattern 11: Context Managers (with statement)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "You need to save weights, open files, acquire locks. Context managers let you do setup/cleanup automatically.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You're saving weights to a file. You need to open it, write data, close it. What if an error happens in the middle?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pickle\n",
    "\n",
    "# Bad Code: Manual cleanup (easy to forget)\n",
    "def save_weights_BAD(weights, filepath):\n",
    "    f = open(filepath, 'wb')\n",
    "    pickle.dump(weights, f)\n",
    "    f.close()  # What if an error happens above?\n",
    "\n",
    "# If an error happens during pickle.dump(), the file never closes!\n",
    "# This is a resource leak."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Good Code: Context manager (automatic cleanup)\n",
    "def save_weights_GOOD(weights, filepath):\n",
    "    with open(filepath, 'wb') as f:\n",
    "        pickle.dump(weights, f)\n",
    "    # File automatically closes, even if an error occurred\n",
    "\n",
    "# The 'with' statement guarantees cleanup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Writing Your Own Context Manager\n",
    "\n",
    "Sometimes you need custom setup/cleanup. Use the `@contextmanager` decorator:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from contextlib import contextmanager\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simple context manager for timing\n",
    "@contextmanager\n",
    "def timer(name):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Context manager that times a block of code.\"\"\"\n",
    "    print(f\"[{name}] Starting...\")\n",
    "    start = time.time()\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        yield  # Code inside 'with' runs here\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        elapsed = time.time() - start\n",
    "        print(f\"[{name}] Done in {elapsed:.3f}s\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Usage\n",
    "with timer(\"Training epoch\"):\n",
    "    time.sleep(0.5)  # Simulate work\n",
    "    print(\"  Training in progress...\")"
   ]
