    "---\n",
    "# PART 5: PRACTICAL ML PATTERNS\n",
    "## Patterns you'll use constantly in neural networks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pattern 12: Slicing (Know When NOT to Slice)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why You Care\n",
    "NumPy slicing is powerful but can be a performance trap. Slicing **creates a copy** by default in pure Python lists, but **views** in NumPy (which is good). Understanding this prevents bugs.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Problem\n",
    "You're batching data. You slice batches from a dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Slicing lists (creates copies)\n",
    "data = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n",
    "batch = data[0:3]  # Creates a new list [1, 2, 3]\n",
    "batch[0] = 999\n",
    "print(f\"Original: {data}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Batch: {batch}\")  # Original unchanged (separate lists)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Slicing NumPy arrays (creates views, not copies)\n",
    "data = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])\n",
    "batch = data[0:3]  # Creates a view (same underlying data)\n",
    "batch[0] = 999\n",
    "print(f\"Original: {data}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Batch: {batch}\")  # Original changed too!\n",
    "\n",
    "# If you want a copy:\n",
    "batch_copy = data[0:3].copy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### When NOT to Slice\n",
    "\n",
    "Slicing repeatedly in a loop is slow. Use indexing instead:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bad Code: Repeated slicing (slow for large arrays)\n",
    "data = np.random.randn(10000, 10)\n",
    "\n",
    "batches = []\n",
    "for i in range(0, len(data), 32):\n",
    "    batch = data[i:i+32]  # Slice\n",
    "    batches.append(batch)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Better: Use a generator (from Pattern 10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Your Turn: Practice\n",
    "\n",
    "What's the difference between these two?\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "arr = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Slice assignment\n",
    "arr[0:2] = [10, 20]\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Index assignment\n",
    "arr[[0, 1]] = [10, 20]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "When would you use each?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
